1
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:11,900
I began this Restoration because my birthright was stolen…

2
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:14,220
and I wanted it back.

3
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:17,140
Not for the people of the Reach,

4
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:19,300
but because it was <b>mine.</b>

5
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:24,020
I wanted war for all the wrong reasons.

6
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:27,300
But on Weldry,

7
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:31,060
I traded that naivete for nobler purpose.

8
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:34,940
Seeing my people's suffering with my own eyes…

9
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:38,340
taught me <b>why</b> I must fight.

10
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:44,180
On Artru I found humility.

11
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:46,980
Blinded by righteousness,

12
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:50,420
I was reckless in my pursuit of power…

13
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:53,420
and it almost cost us the war.

14
00:00:58,060 --> 00:00:59,540
On Guldra

15
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:02,740
I learned to steel my heart.

16
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:06,340
I chose necessity over conscience.

17
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:09,940
A choice… that nearly broke me.

18
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:20,300
Finally, on Coromodir, the world of my birth,

19
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:22,340
I found resolve -

20
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:25,980
and, standing over my cousin's broken body…

21
00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:27,420
victory.

22
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:31,220
Only through these lessons, paid for in blood,

23
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:34,100
did I become a ruler worthy of title.

24
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:37,620
A High Lady prepared to sit the Cormorant Throne.

25
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:39,900
The Protector of Coromodir.

26
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:42,540
The Sword of Restoration.

27
00:01:45,380 --> 00:01:48,740
But this question still plagues me:

28
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:50,700
am I a hero?

29
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:54,580
Did I sacrifice too much at the altar of victory?

30
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:57,420
Do my triumphs outweigh my mistakes?

31
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:02,020
War is a clash between conscience and necessity,

32
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:05,940
an ocean of chaos and bloody compromise.

33
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:10,100
War shapes history,

34
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:14,540
and history chooses its heroes.

35
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:22,580
As for you, mercenary…

36
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:26,820
<b>You</b> made the liberation of the Aurigan Reach a reality.

37
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:31,100
Every trial I faced would have been my last

38
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:33,420
without your skill on the battlefield.

39
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:39,540
I still don't know if you fought for honor,

40
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:41,340
or for the thrill of it.

41
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:45,220
For belief in my cause, or just my money.

42
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:50,420
But whether it was your noble heart or mercenary mind…

43
00:02:50,860 --> 00:02:52,660
your actions gave us hope.

44
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:56,540
That makes you a hero in the eyes of history.

45
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:00,220
And you know what?

46
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:03,820
It doesn't matter if <b>you</b> believe it.

47
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:05,820
Because others do,

48
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:10,180
as I believed in the heroes of my father's stories.

49
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:13,860
After all,

50
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:15,900
when we are gone…

51
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:22,540
Stories are what remain.

